From 8a453289bf3ec14b7b0f7cd46890b58337e44218 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: telegdyd <telegdyd93@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:00:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] jasmine: render tickets for libsweetca mode 2 (j0101)

Task 16 build 2, behind sweetgpu_tickets=1 (needs sweetfb_queue=1, default
off). SweetGPU selector 8 QUERY/BEGIN and 9 SEAL/ABORT: a generation per
written IOSurface, sealed with a successful post-BEGIN submit's seqno, so
CoreAnimation's w_Flush can return without draining the driver queue. The
presenter shows a ticketed layer once it is sealed and the GPU has passed
that seqno; CPU access to a pending surface waits for it (100 ms).
Cancellation on GPU client close and display power-off; terminal receipts
bounded per connection; framebench events 30/31/37-41.

A slow frame is not a fault: tickets have no deadline of their own (BEGIN is
the first draw, so CA's CPU work and shader variants compiled in the drain
count against it); the presenter's bound for ticketed frames is 1 s.

Implementation by Codex (gpt-6.1-sol), review fixes by Claude.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
